.TH geectl-pull-request-request-changes 1  "geectl-pull-request-request-changes 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-pull\-request\-request\-changes \- Ask for changes on a pull request, as `approve` but with the review declined instead of accepted. Dry\-run by default; mutates only with `\-\-live`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl pull\-request request\-changes\fR [\fB\-\-message\fR] [\fB\-\-user\fR] [\fB\-\-group\fR] [\fB\-\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-package\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIREFERENCE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ask for changes on a pull request, as `approve` but with the review declined instead of accepted. Dry\-run by default; mutates only with `\-\-live`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-message\fR \fI<MESSAGE>\fR
The message left with the review. Values starting with `\-` are taken literally: a message may open with a `\- ` bullet
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fI<USER>\fR
Act on the review asked of this user (OBS only)
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fI<GROUP>\fR
Act on the review asked of this group (OBS only)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
Act on the review asked of this project (OBS only)
.TP
\fB\-\-package\fR \fI<PACKAGE>\fR
Act on the review asked of this package (OBS only; needs its project)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIREFERENCE\fR>
The pull\-request handle: `obs:<id>` or `gitea:<owner>/<repo>#<number>`
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
